   "subject": "Newbie question: what files in packrat do I check in to git",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I don&#39;t want to check in src or lib, because<div><br></div><div>1) they are large and</div><div>2) I don&#39;t own them</div><div><br></div><div>So what files do I check in?</div><div><br></div><div>-Alex</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "WASTdOEJZrYJ",
   "from": "Kevin Ushey",
   "author": "ab0d2be2ea8dabe8",
   "date": "2015-02-05T19:17:40Z",
   "subject": "Re: Newbie question: what files in packrat do I check in to git",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">At minimum, you need to check in the <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">packrat/packrat.lock</code> file — Packrat should know how to restore based on that, unless you are using packages within local repositories not available on other system. You should also check in the project <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">.Rprofile</code> as well as <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">packrat/init.R</code>, to ensure that we automatically enter packrat mode upon starting an R session in that directory. Finally, you should also check in the <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">packrat/packrat.opts</code> file, although this is not strictly necessary.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">When calling <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">packrat::restore()</code> from an empty project with just a lockfile, Packrat will automatically find, download, and install packages as needed (presuming it can locate them)</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">Thanks,<br>Kevin</p></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">On Wednesday, February 4, 2015 at 4:46:56 PM UTC-8, Alex Brown wrote:</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\"></p><div><p></p><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">I don&#39;t want to check in src or lib, because<div><br></div><div>1) they are large and</div><div>2) I don&#39;t own them</div><div><br></div><div>So what files do I check in?</div><div><br></div><div>-Alex</div></div></blockquote><p></p></div><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\"></p>\r\n<div title=\"MDH:QXQgbWluaW11bSwgeW91IG5lZWQgdG8gY2hlY2sgaW4gdGhlIGBwYWNrcmF0L3BhY2tyYXQubG9j\r\na2AgZmlsZSAtLSBQYWNrcmF0IHNob3VsZCBrbm93IGhvdyB0byByZXN0b3JlIGJhc2VkIG9uIHRo\r\nYXQsIHVubGVzcyB5b3UgYXJlIHVzaW5nIHBhY2thZ2VzIHdpdGhpbiBsb2NhbCByZXBvc2l0b3Jp\r\nZXMgbm90IGF2YWlsYWJsZSBvbiBvdGhlciBzeXN0ZW0uIFlvdSBzaG91bGQgYWxzbyBjaGVjayBp\r\nbiB0aGUgcHJvamVjdCBgLlJwcm9maWxlYCBhcyB3ZWxsIGFzIGBwYWNrcmF0L2luaXQuUmAsIHRv\r\nIGVuc3VyZSB0aGF0IHdlIGF1dG9tYXRpY2FsbHkgZW50ZXIgcGFja3JhdCBtb2RlIHVwb24gc3Rh\r\ncnRpbmcgYW4gUiBzZXNzaW9uIGluIHRoYXQgZGlyZWN0b3J5LiBGaW5hbGx5LCB5b3Ugc2hvdWxk\r\nIGFsc28gY2hlY2sgaW4gdGhlIGBwYWNrcmF0L3BhY2tyYXQub3B0c2AgZmlsZSwgYWx0aG91Z2gg\r\ndGhpcyBpcyBub3Qgc3RyaWN0bHkgbmVjZXNzYXJ5LjxkaXY+PGJyPjwvZGl2PjxkaXY+V2hlbiBj\r\nYWxsaW5nIGBwYWNrcmF0OjpyZXN0b3JlKClgIGZyb20gYW4gZW1wdHkgcHJvamVjdCB3aXRoIGp1\r\nc3QgYSBsb2NrZmlsZSwgUGFja3JhdCB3aWxsIGF1dG9tYXRpY2FsbHkgZmluZCwgZG93bmxvYWQs\r\nIGFuZCBpbnN0YWxsIHBhY2thZ2VzIGFzIG5lZWRlZCAocHJlc3VtaW5nIGl0IGNhbiBsb2NhdGUg\r\ndGhlbSk8L2Rpdj48ZGl2Pjxicj48L2Rpdj48ZGl2PlRoYW5rcyw8L2Rpdj48ZGl2PktldmluPGJy\r\nPjxicj5PbiBXZWRuZXNkYXksIEZlYnJ1YXJ5IDQsIDIwMTUgYXQgNDo0Njo1NiBQTSBVVEMtOCwg\r\nQWxleCBCcm93biB3cm90ZTo8YmxvY2txdW90ZSBjbGFzcz0iZ21haWxfcXVvdGUiIHN0eWxlPSJt\r\nYXJnaW46IDA7bWFyZ2luLWxlZnQ6IDAuOGV4O2JvcmRlci1sZWZ0OiAxcHggI2NjYyBzb2xpZDtw\r\nYWRkaW5nLWxlZnQ6IDFleDsiPjxkaXYgZGlyPSJsdHIiPkkgZG9uJ3Qgd2FudCB0byBjaGVj